	(text_box "VCAP_M_TAP input: 100 kOhm + 10 nF, OPA333 zero-drift follower"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 178.8 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9293431b-cf7b-5bfa-99fc-d7a812526078")
	)
	(text_box "VCAP_M_TAP = Vcap x 40.3 k / (40.2 M + 40.3 k) = Vcap / 998.5 (string on 11). 1,950 V -> 1.953 V; 2,200 V -> 2.203 V; 60 V -> 60.1 mV.\nR701 100 kOhm meets R7 (reader may be unpowered while the capacitor is charged): tap clamp 3.6 V on 11 -> at most (3.6 - 0) / 110 k = 33 uA into U704's input\nclamp diodes (OPA333 abs. max. +-1 mA, SBOS351E 6.1). No extra clamp here: any diode added would leak into the 50 kOhm source.\nR701 + C701 (10 nF C0G): 1.6 ms time constant, -3 dB 159 Hz. Lag during a charge: 205 V/s x 1.6 ms = 0.3 V (within the 1 ms loop's 0.2 V overshoot budget,\n§B4.4).\nU704 OPA333: Vos 10 uV max, 0.05 uV/K; IB 200 pA max at 25 C, 150 pA typ over temperature (SBOS351E 6.6) -> 1 nA assumed worst case x 150 kOhm source = 0.15\nmV = 0.15 V of capacitor voltage. Output swing to the negative rail is the limit near 0 V: readings below about 10 mV (10 V) are not linear [UNVERIFIED at\nthis load].\nR702 1 MOhm to 3V3_MAIN at the follower output: a failed-open follower output reads FULL SCALE (over-voltage, LOWV_OK low = not permitted) rather than 0 V.\nThe follower sinks 3.3 uA at the LOWV threshold."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 178.8 23.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3f7a1a63-d90b-5456-9202-5dba7ceb76be")
	)
